<title>INDIA: Indian bullion markets closed for local holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian bullion markets closed for local holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's gold and silver markets remained shut on Tuesday for the Jain festival holiday, dealers said. They reopen on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They were closed on Monday.</p>
<p>On Friday, Indian silver erased some early losses on the back of industrial and seasonal buying but a weak global trend kept prices lower, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
